  "body": "## Cause\n\nThe post-merge batch gate failed in step 1, `debug build (--no-run)` (runs 43935486746 and 43935744100). The cause is in test code only. Product code builds.\n\n1. PR #2140 (EDM wire tool) added two tests with a `CuttingRow` literal of the old shape. PR #2101 (it includes #2015) made `material` an `Option<WorkMaterial>` and added `stepdown` and `stepover`. Each PR built alone. After the two merges, these targets do not compile:\n   - `crates/tools/src/wire.rs:103` (lib test of `camcraft-tools`)\n   - `crates/app/tests/wire_tool.rs:106` (test `wire_tool` of `camcraft-app`)\n2. After the build is fixed, a test fails. PR #2215 added `testdata/models/fig8.step` without a row in the STEP agreement bench. `step_files_agree_or_refuse_by_name` fails with `a fixture has no row, or a row has no fixture - re-triage`.\n\nThe xtask gate change of #1952 is not the cause.\n\n## What changed\n\n- The two wire tests build the row with `CuttingRow::plain(Some(WorkMaterial::MildSteel), 0.0, <feed>)`. Each test keeps its \"EDM conditions\" refusal assertion.\n- `crates/kernel/tests/step_agreement.rs` has a row for `fig8.step` and the per-file test `step_fig8`. The row pins the reading that the bench gives: `solidcore refuses: #14 at read: pcurves failed on`, `no exact solid to judge against`. This is the same class as `fillet_corner.step`.\n\nNo safety check or refusal is removed.\n\n## Readings and tests\n\n- The batch build step `cargo test -j 6 -p camcraft-geometry -p camcraft-kernel -p camcraft-cl -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --no-run`: exit 0 on Windows.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick` on the first commit: 409 steps (all suites of the touched crates), 1 failed (`kernel suites: step_agreement`, cause 2 above). The run was marked VOID because the tree changed at its end (my second edit).\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --failed gate-logs/quick-20261116-193211` on the final head: `kernel suites: step_agreement` ok (19 passed).\n- `camcraft-app --test wire_tool`: 5 passed. `camcraft-tools --lib wire`: 1 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-kernel --all-targets -- -D warnings` and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test wire_tool -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nPinned by: `wire_tool_command_refuses_bad_rpm_diameter_corner_and_cutting_rows_by_name`, the `wire` lib test of `camcraft-tools`, `step_fig8`, `step_files_agree_or_refuse_by_name`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The Linux runner. The build and the tests ran on Windows only.\n- The ui suites and clippy of the full batch tier. The post-merge gate runs them after the merge.\n- The cause of the solidcore pcurve refusal on `fig8.step`. The row only records the reading.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #2244\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
